{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured persistent daily rotation for /var/log/inventory/app.log with seven compressed rotations. Verified continued writing through an open descriptor, then rebooted node1 and confirmed full recovery with a changed boot ID.","actions_performed":["Installed /etc/logrotate.d/inventory-app using daily, rotate 7, compress, missingok, notifempty, and copytruncate.","Validated the configuration with the installed legacy logrotate version.","Performed a live rotation and confirmed compressed output plus uninterrupted application-style writing.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified configuration, cron, active and rotated logs, kernel, and write behavior after recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Rotate app.log daily and retain seven compressed rotations","command_ids":["cmd-9a419e4ad5024698","cmd-c4a3995c896f45a4","cmd-b5b32c54f8664db2"],"summary":"The installed parser reports daily rotation with seven retained copies; a live rotation created a valid compressed app.log.1.gz, and the rule persisted after reboot."},{"requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation","command_ids":["cmd-c4a3995c896f45a4"],"summary":"The log inode remained unchanged across rotation, and a write through the descriptor opened before rotation appeared in the active log afterward."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed OS release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-186964f73c4e40c3","cmd-b5b32c54f8664db2"],"summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 remained installed and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic was unchanged after reboot."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart and recovery for node1","command_ids":["cmd-aa5e1ad24b3e4a17","cmd-fa34202efd8f4575","cmd-fc00030b9be84577","cmd-b5b32c54f8664db2"],"summary":"Captured healthy baseline boot d844f8dc-5326-4df3-aacd-a6ed38380f35, received reboot acknowledgement, observed new boot 0b3d084f-3f7e-4553-b6a1-64b014fb2f2b, and verified cron, configuration, current data, compressed data, and new writes recovered."}]}
